<p local-id=3D"e4883219f75e"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,0);">Semantics: =
see use case</span></p>
<p local-id=3D"a9b6af89cc1b"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,0);">Analysis: B=
e aware that in BMM, like in BTM(T) the .I element indicates the active bag=
 segment (and hence sets the carrying segment). The event =E2=80=9Crealizes=
=E2=80=9D when bag is actually loaded on the aircraft. Hence process is map=
ped to T;Load;Load</span></p>
<p local-id=3D"6fd403f07681"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,0);">Result: </s=
pan><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://iataonline.sharepoint.com/:u=
:/r/sites/IATABaggageWorkingGroup/Shared%20Documents/Baggage%20Information%=
20Exchange%20(BIX)%20Sub%20Group/Taskforce%20best%20practices%20BIX%20v2/Sa=
mples/source%20RP1745/9.9.1%20Loaded%20bag.xml?d=3Dwd3e7c8ea54a74bada18120e=
abb62eeb2&amp;csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3D8gGbjc" rel=3D"nofollow">9.9.1 Lo=
aded bag</a></p>
